notes.body:
Here's the example for column freezing and pinning a packet to the top. This change started off as a want to freeze columns, and packets. Like in Excel, the intent was to freeze a row, and scrolling would only occur below that. After I prototyped that, the usability was terrible. While in this process though there as test that happen to move the the packet to the top. As I moved to this route, I did have some limitations that caused me to create the proxy for the view to be at the top. I landed on limiting the total number of packets to 10 (I could make this configurable). I've tested this on ubuntu with 600Mb captures, and several other captures. Every thing performed as expected. please take a look and let me know what you think.

![image](/uploads/cc7f2f46ff0d9bb5489a05decf00ccfb/image.png){width=748 height=600}

Pinned packet example

![image](/uploads/b4500fec11d4f0fcba57332a1a610cb1/image.png){width=480 height=385}

